IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 (Cth) -- the elector: who is entitled to enrolment and to vote (s 93), enrolment for an
-- address after a month's residence (s 99(1), (2)), age 16 enrolment (s 100), compulsory enrolment, transfer and change of
-- address, with their offences and the bars on proceedings (s 101), compulsory voting, the penalty notice, the $20 penalty and
-- the offences of failing to vote and of a false response (s 245). Section 4(1) ("Elector") is worked out from the facts.
--
-- SEAT: the elector -- the person who must enrol and vote, and who is sent the penalty notice. Every decision is phrased as
-- that person would ask it ("Must I enrol", "Must I vote", "What can I pay to keep it out of court"). The candidate's
-- questions are in cea-candidate.l4.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 81, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 16, 2025 (register id
-- C2026C00260, in 2 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1918A00027.txt. No regulation is used: the
-- Commonwealth Electoral Regulation 2016 is not deposited, and nothing in these sections takes a number or date from it (the
-- "prescribed time" in s 245 is, by s 245(18), the time stated in the notice). The value of a penalty unit is set by the
-- Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, not by this Act, and is an INPUT.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Rolls and Divisions themselves and their redistribution; Antarctic, eligible overseas and itinerant electors
-- (ss 94-96) beyond their exclusion from s 245; provisional enrolment of applicants for citizenship (ss 99A, 99B); direct
-- enrolment by the Commissioner (ss 103A, 103B) beyond its bar on proceedings; silent enrolment (s 104); objections and review
-- (Parts IX, X); polling and how to vote (Parts XV-XVII); the second-tier steps the DRO takes on the lists (s 245(2), (12),
-- (13)); s 245(11) (another elector responding for an absent or incapacitated one); s 245(16) (who may prosecute).
-- Every qualification other than age and residence is taken to have held throughout, so the day of entitlement is worked out
-- from the 18th birthday and the month at the address only; a person who became a citizen after both is not modelled (see
-- NOTES.md).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 -- the elector`

-- Where my name is on the Rolls. "Roll" is the Roll for a Subdivision (s 4(1), s 81); "Subdivision" is the Act's term for the
-- part of a Division whose Roll an address belongs to.
DECLARE `My enrolment` IS ONE OF
    `not on the Roll`
    `on the Roll for my address`
    `on the Roll for an old address in another Subdivision`
    `on the Roll for an old address in the same Subdivision`

-- The facts the elector can state. A borrowed term (temporary visa, unlawful non-citizen: Migration Act 1958) is asked as a
-- fact, not worked out.
DECLARE `My circumstances` HAS
    `my date of birth`                                                   IS A DATE
    `I am an Australian citizen`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a British subject who was on a roll immediately before 26 January 1984` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a temporary visa or am an unlawful non-citizen`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I cannot understand enrolment and voting because of cognitive impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was convicted of treason or treachery and have not been pardoned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am serving a sentence of imprisonment of 3 years or longer`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day I began living at my address`                               IS A DATE
    `my enrolment`                                                       IS A `My enrolment`
    `I am an Antarctic, eligible overseas or itinerant elector`          IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Age`

-- The Act says "attained 18 years of age" (s 93(1)(a)), "turned 16" (s 100(1)(a)). INFERENCE (the Act does not say): a person
-- attains an age at the start of the anniversary of birth; a birthday of 29 February is taken as 28 February in other years
-- (daydate's `add years` clamps).
@export Have I reached a given age on a given day?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances; only your date of birth is read
      `the age` IS A NUMBER             @desc The age in whole years
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day to test, ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-05-03
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I reached the age` IF
    Day `the day` AT LEAST Day (`add years` (`me`'s `my date of birth`) `the age`)

§§ `93 -- persons entitled to enrolment and to vote`

-- s 93(1): "all persons: (a) who have attained 18 years of age; and (b) who are: (i) Australian citizens; or (ii) persons
-- (other than Australian citizens) who would ... be British subjects ... and whose names were, immediately before 26 January
-- 1984" on a roll "shall be entitled to enrolment". (7): the holder of a temporary visa, or an unlawful non-citizen, "is not
-- entitled to enrolment". (8): a person who "(a) by reason of cognitive impairment, is incapable of understanding the nature
-- and significance of enrolment and voting; or (b) has been convicted of treason or treachery and has not been pardoned" is not
-- entitled to be placed or kept on any Roll or to vote.
@export Apart from my age, am I qualified for enrolment (s 93(1)(b), (7), (8))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I qualified for enrolment apart from age` IF
        (    `me`'s `I am an Australian citizen`
         OR  `me`'s `I am a British subject who was on a roll immediately before 26 January 1984`)
    AND NOT `me`'s `I hold a temporary visa or am an unlawful non-citizen`
    AND NOT `me`'s `I cannot understand enrolment and voting because of cognitive impairment`
    AND NOT `me`'s `I was convicted of treason or treachery and have not been pardoned`

@export Am I entitled to enrolment on a given day (s 93(1))?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day to test, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to enrolment` IF
        `Have I reached the age` `me` 18 `the day`
    AND `Am I qualified for enrolment apart from age` `me`

-- s 93(2): "an elector whose name is on the Roll for a Division is entitled to vote" at the Senate and House elections for it.
-- (3), (4): a person enrolled on a s 100 claim who "has not attained 18 years of age on the date fixed for the polling" is not
-- entitled to vote, and "shall not be taken to be ... enrolled on a Roll" for that election. (8AA): a person "serving a
-- sentence of imprisonment of 3 years or longer is not entitled to vote".
@export Am I entitled to vote at an election with this polling day (s 93(2)-(4), (8), (8AA))?
GIVEN `me`             IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the polling day` IS A DATE              @desc The date fixed for the polling, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to vote at the election` IF
        NOT `me`'s `my enrolment` EQUALS `not on the Roll`
    AND `Am I entitled to enrolment` `me` `the polling day`
    AND NOT `me`'s `I am serving a sentence of imprisonment of 3 years or longer`

§§ `99 -- enrolment for an address`

-- s 99(1): "Any person qualified for enrolment, who lives at an address in a Subdivision, and has lived at that address for a
-- period of one month last past, shall be entitled ... to have his or her name placed on the Roll for that Subdivision."
-- (2): an elector on the Roll for one Subdivision who has lived a month at an address in another "shall be entitled ... to have
-- his or her name transferred". "One month" is read as one calendar month from the day residence began (INFERENCE).
@export Have I lived at my address for one month on a given day (s 99)?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances; the day you began living at your address is read
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day to test, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I lived at my address for a month` IF
    Day `the day` AT LEAST Day (`add months` (`me`'s `the day I began living at my address`) 1)

@export Am I entitled to be on the Roll for my address on a given day (s 99(1), (2))?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day to test, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to be on the Roll for my address` IF
        `Am I entitled to enrolment` `me` `the day`
    AND `Have I lived at my address for a month` `me` `the day`

-- The day the entitlement in s 99 begins: the later of the 18th birthday and a month at the address. Every other
-- qualification is taken to have held throughout (see the header).
@export On what day did I become entitled to be on the Roll for my address (s 99)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day did I become entitled to be on the Roll for my address` IS
    IF Day `my 18th birthday` AT LEAST Day `a month at my address`
    THEN `my 18th birthday`
    ELSE `a month at my address`
    WHERE
        `my 18th birthday`     MEANS `add years` (`me`'s `my date of birth`) 18
        `a month at my address` MEANS `add months` (`me`'s `the day I began living at my address`) 1

§§ `100 -- age 16 enrolment`

-- s 100(1): a person who "(a) has turned 16, but is under 18, years of age; and (b) would be entitled, in respect of residence
-- at an address, to be enrolled for a Subdivision if he or she were 18 years of age; may send or deliver a claim". The Act
-- calls this "age 16 enrolment"; the Act's "provisional" enrolment (ss 99A, 99B) is for applicants for citizenship. It is a
-- right, not a duty: s 101(1) excepts a person entitled "by virtue of section ... 100".
@export May I claim age 16 enrolment now that I am 16 or 17 (s 100)?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day you would claim, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I claim age 16 enrolment` IF
        `Have I reached the age` `me` 16 `the day`
    AND NOT `Have I reached the age` `me` 18 `the day`
    AND `Am I qualified for enrolment apart from age` `me`
    AND `Have I lived at my address for a month` `me` `the day`
    AND NOT `me`'s `my enrolment` EQUALS `on the Roll for my address`

§§ `101 -- compulsory enrolment and transfer`

-- s 101(1): "Every person who is entitled to be enrolled for any Subdivision, otherwise than by virtue of section 94, 94A, 95,
-- 96 or 100, whether by way of enrolment or transfer of enrolment, and whose name is not on the Roll, shall forthwith fill in
-- and sign a claim and send or deliver the claim to the Electoral Commissioner."
@export Must I enrol, or transfer my enrolment, now (s 101(1))?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc Today, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I enrol or transfer my enrolment` IF
        `Am I entitled to be on the Roll for my address` `me` `the day`
    AND (    `me`'s `my enrolment` EQUALS `not on the Roll`
         OR  `me`'s `my enrolment` EQUALS `on the Roll for an old address in another Subdivision`)

-- s 101(4): a person entitled "whose name is not on the Roll upon the expiration of 21 days from the date upon which the person
-- became so entitled, or at any subsequent date while the person continues to be so entitled, commits an offence unless he or
-- she proves that the non-enrolment is not in consequence of his or her failure to send or deliver" a claim. INFERENCE on the
-- count: the 21 days run from the day after the day of entitlement, so the last day off the Roll without the offence is that
-- day plus 21. NOTHING if I am not qualified apart from age, so that no day of entitlement comes.
@export What is the last day I can be off the Roll for my address without committing the s 101(4) offence?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day I can be off the Roll without an offence` IS
    IF `Am I qualified for enrolment apart from age` `me`
    THEN JUST (`On what day did I become entitled to be on the Roll for my address` `me` PLUS 21)
    ELSE NOTHING

@export Have I committed the s 101(4) offence of not being on the Roll?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day to test, ISO 8601
      `I can prove it is not because I failed to send a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can prove that you are off the Roll for some reason other than your own failure to send a filled-in, signed claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the offence of not enrolling` IF
        `Must I enrol or transfer my enrolment` `me` `the day`
    AND Day `the day` GREATER THAN Day (`On what day did I become entitled to be on the Roll for my address` `me` PLUS 21)
    AND NOT `I can prove it is not because I failed to send a claim`

-- s 101(7): once a claim is sent, "proceedings shall not be instituted against that person for any offence against subsection
-- (1) or (4) committed before the claim was so sent". (8): nor once "the Electoral Commissioner enters a person's name or address
-- in a Roll under section 103A or 103B".
@export Can I be prosecuted for not enrolling (s 101(4), (7), (8))?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day of the offence, ISO 8601
      `I can prove it is not because I failed to send a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can prove that you are off the Roll for some reason other than your own failure to send a claim
      `I have since sent a claim`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have sent or delivered a claim for enrolment since then
      `the Commissioner has since enrolled me directly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Electoral Commissioner has since entered you on the Roll without a claim (ss 103A, 103B)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be prosecuted for not enrolling` IF
        `Have I committed the offence of not enrolling` `me` `the day` `I can prove it is not because I failed to send a claim`
    AND NOT `I have since sent a claim`
    AND NOT `the Commissioner has since enrolled me directly`

-- s 101(5): a person enrolled who "(a) has changed his or her place of living from one address in that Subdivision to another
-- address in the same Subdivision; and (b) has lived at the new address for a period of one month; ... must, within 21 days
-- after the end of the period referred to in paragraph (b), give written notice of the new address". (6A): no offence if
-- "the person has not reached the age of 18 years".
@export Must I tell the Electoral Commissioner my new address in the same Subdivision (s 101(5))?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc Today, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give notice of my new address` IF
        `me`'s `my enrolment` EQUALS `on the Roll for an old address in the same Subdivision`
    AND `Have I lived at my address for a month` `me` `the day`

@export By when must I give written notice of my new address in the same Subdivision (s 101(5))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give notice of my new address` IS
    `add months` (`me`'s `the day I began living at my address`) 1 PLUS 21

@export If I am late telling the Commissioner my new address, is it an offence for me (s 101(5), (6), (6A))?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day to test, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it an offence that I have not given notice of my new address` IF
        `Must I give notice of my new address` `me` `the day`
    AND Day `the day` GREATER THAN Day (`By when must I give notice of my new address` `me`)
    AND `Have I reached the age` `me` 18 `the day`

§§ `245 -- compulsory voting`

-- s 245(1): "It shall be the duty of every elector to vote at each election." s 4(1): "Elector means any person whose name
-- appears on a Roll as an elector." s 245(17): in this section elector "does not include: (a) an Antarctic elector; or (b) an
-- eligible overseas elector; or (c) an itinerant elector". s 93(4): a person under 18 on polling day is not taken to be
-- enrolled for that election.
@export Am I an elector bound by compulsory voting at an election with this polling day (ss 4(1), 93(4), 245(17))?
GIVEN `me`             IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the polling day` IS A DATE              @desc The polling day, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an elector for compulsory voting` IF
        NOT `me`'s `my enrolment` EQUALS `not on the Roll`
    AND `Have I reached the age` `me` 18 `the polling day`
    AND NOT `me`'s `I am an Antarctic, eligible overseas or itinerant elector`

-- INFERENCE (not express): a person who is not entitled to vote (s 93(8), (8AA)) has no duty to vote; s 245(4)(c) lets the
-- DRO withhold a notice from one who "was ineligible to vote at the election".
@export Must I vote at an election with this polling day (s 245(1))?
GIVEN `me`             IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the polling day` IS A DATE              @desc The polling day, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I vote` IF
        `Am I an elector for compulsory voting` `me` `the polling day`
    AND `Am I entitled to vote at the election` `me` `the polling day`

-- What happened at one election, as the elector can state it, with the one judgment the Act hands to the DRO.
DECLARE `What happened at the election` HAS
    `I voted`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was absent from Australia on polling day`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had a valid and sufficient reason for not voting`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `I believe it is part of my religious duty to abstain from voting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the DRO is satisfied of my absence, ineligibility or reason` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 245(14): "the fact that an elector believes it to be part of his or her religious duty to abstain from voting constitutes a
-- valid and sufficient reason". The subsection is "without limiting" what else may be one.
@export Do I have a valid and sufficient reason for not voting (s 245(14))?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened at the election` @desc What happened at the election
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a valid and sufficient reason` IF
        `what happened`'s `I had a valid and sufficient reason for not voting`
    OR  `what happened`'s `I believe it is part of my religious duty to abstain from voting`

-- s 245(2), (3): the Commissioner lists "the electors who appear to have failed to vote", and within 3 months after polling day
-- each DRO "must" send a penalty notice to each. (4): "The DRO is not required to send or deliver a penalty notice if he or she
-- is satisfied that the elector: (a) is dead; or (b) was absent from Australia on polling day; or (c) was ineligible to vote at
-- the election; or (d) had a valid and sufficient reason for failing to vote." The DRO's satisfaction is an input, answered
-- conditionally. Paragraph (a) is not a question the elector asks.
@export Must the DRO send me a penalty notice for not voting (s 245(2)-(4))?
GIVEN `me`             IS A `My circumstances`              @desc Your circumstances
      `the polling day` IS A DATE                           @desc The polling day, ISO 8601
      `what happened`   IS A `What happened at the election` @desc What happened at the election
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be sent a penalty notice` IF
        `Am I an elector for compulsory voting` `me` `the polling day`
    AND NOT `what happened`'s `I voted`
    AND NOT (    `what happened`'s `the DRO is satisfied of my absence, ineligibility or reason`
             AND (    `what happened`'s `I was absent from Australia on polling day`
                  OR  NOT `Am I entitled to vote at the election` `me` `the polling day`
                  OR  `Do I have a valid and sufficient reason` `what happened`))

@export By when must any penalty notice for not voting be sent to me (s 245(3))?
GIVEN `the polling day` IS A DATE @desc The polling day, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must a penalty notice be sent to me` IS `add months` `the polling day` 3

-- s 245(5)(c): to keep the apparent failure out of court the elector may, within the time stated in the notice (s 245(18)),
-- "(i) if the elector did vote ... give the DRO particulars ...; or (ii) if the elector failed to vote--give the DRO a valid and
-- sufficient reason for the failure; or (iii) pay to the DRO a penalty of $20." (9): if the DRO is not satisfied, a further
-- notice offers the same $20. The $20 is written into the Act; s 321 does not index it.
@export How much can I pay to keep my failure to vote out of court (s 245(5)(c)(iii), (9)(d)), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What can I pay to keep my failure to vote out of court` IS 20

-- s 245(6): if the elector "does not respond to a penalty notice in the manner indicated ... within the prescribed time, the
-- DRO must" send a second penalty notice.
@export If I was sent a penalty notice, must I be sent a second one (s 245(6))?
GIVEN `I responded in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave particulars of voting, gave a reason, or paid the $20 within the time stated in the first notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be sent a second penalty notice` IF NOT `I responded in time`

-- s 245(15): "An elector commits an offence if the elector fails to vote at an election." (15B): not "if the elector has a valid
-- and sufficient reason for the failure".
@export Have I committed the offence of failing to vote (s 245(15), (15B))?
GIVEN `me`             IS A `My circumstances`              @desc Your circumstances
      `the polling day` IS A DATE                           @desc The polling day, ISO 8601
      `what happened`   IS A `What happened at the election` @desc What happened at the election
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the offence of failing to vote` IF
        `Must I vote` `me` `the polling day`
    AND NOT `what happened`'s `I voted`
    AND NOT `Do I have a valid and sufficient reason` `what happened`

-- s 245(8): proceedings for a contravention of (15) "are prohibited" if, within the prescribed time, the DRO is satisfied by the
-- elector's response that the elector voted or had a valid and sufficient reason, or the elector pays the $20. (10): the same
-- if the $20 is paid in time in response to a notice under (9).
@export Can I no longer be prosecuted for failing to vote (s 245(8), (10))?
GIVEN `the DRO accepted my response in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within the time in the notice, you gave particulars of voting or a reason and the DRO was satisfied by it
      `I paid the $20 in time`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid the $20 penalty within the time stated in a penalty notice or a further notice under s 245(9)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are proceedings against me for not voting barred` IF
        `the DRO accepted my response in time`
    OR  `I paid the $20 in time`

§§ `101(6), 245(15), (15C) -- the offences, as a table`

-- The elector's offences under these sections. s 101(6): "a fine not exceeding 1 penalty unit"; (6AA) strict liability for (1)
-- and (5); (6AB) absolute liability for (4). s 245(15): "Penalty: 1 penalty unit"; (15A) strict liability. s 245(15C): a
-- statement in response to a penalty notice "that is, to his or her knowledge, false or misleading in a material particular";
-- "Penalty: 1 penalty unit". Nothing makes (15C) strict, so fault must be proved (Criminal Code default; INFERENCE).
DECLARE `My offence` IS ONE OF
    `not enrolling forthwith, s 101(1)`
    `not on the Roll after 21 days, s 101(4)`
    `not giving notice of a new address, s 101(5)`
    `failing to vote, s 245(15)`
    `a false or misleading response to a penalty notice, s 245(15C)`

DECLARE `Liability` IS ONE OF `strict liability`, `absolute liability`, `fault must be proved`

DECLARE `Offence row` HAS
    `penalty units` IS A NUMBER
    `liability`     IS A `Liability`

@export What is the most I can be fined for this offence, and what must be proved (ss 101(6), 245(15), (15C))?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence` @desc The offence: not enrolling (s 101(1) or (4)), not giving notice of a new address (s 101(5)), failing to vote (s 245(15)), or a false response (s 245(15C))
GIVETH AN `Offence row`
DECIDE `The penalty table` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not enrolling forthwith, s 101(1)`                            THEN `Offence row` OF 1, `strict liability`
    WHEN `not on the Roll after 21 days, s 101(4)`                      THEN `Offence row` OF 1, `absolute liability`
    WHEN `not giving notice of a new address, s 101(5)`                 THEN `Offence row` OF 1, `strict liability`
    WHEN `failing to vote, s 245(15)`                                   THEN `Offence row` OF 1, `strict liability`
    WHEN `a false or misleading response to a penalty notice, s 245(15C)` THEN `Offence row` OF 1, `fault must be proved`

@export What is the most I can be fined for this offence, in penalty units?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence` @desc The offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined in penalty units` IS (`The penalty table` `the offence`)'s `penalty units`

-- The value of a penalty unit is set by the Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, not by this Act: an INPUT.
@export What is the most I can be fined for this offence, in dollars?
GIVEN `the offence`                IS A `My offence` @desc The offence
      `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER      @desc The dollar value of one Commonwealth penalty unit on the day of the offence (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined in dollars` IS
    `What is the most I can be fined in penalty units` `the offence` TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`
